  "query_preview": "..\nSYNOPTIC SETUP:\n\nLarge upper trough currently over the Gulf of Alaska will keep the\narea under a generally SW flow with some shortwave ridges through\nmost of the week. That will mean temperatures will be above normal\nwith a couple disturbances bringing the chances of showers/storms.\n\nThe first disturbance moves in Wednesday that looks to mainly\naffect the SE zones as it moves NE into ND.\n\nThursday looks to be the warmest day this week with highs in the\n80s area-wide, a good 10-20 degrees above normal!\n\nThe trough will help to spin up a strong surface low over Alberta\nby Saturday. A brief shower is possible with or ahead of a cold\nfront moving through but is looks like wind and cooler air moving\nin will be the main weather elements as a strong dry slot moves in \nSaturday. A Lake Wind Advisory will probably be needed for Friday\nand Saturday.\n\nLook for temperatures to be cooler Sunday and Monday with the\nchance of showers as an upper disturbance moves in.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nConfidence with temperatures and the potential for windy\nconditions Saturday seem to be increasing as the strong incoming\nsystem should help force these conditions. Confidence in the\nintensity of the showers over the weekend remains low.\n\nOtherwise, generally followed what NBM gave for numbers. TFJ",
